{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "RugRadar",
    "version": "1.2.0",
    "description": "Token danger warnings for agents, paid per call with x402 (USDC on Solana, Base, Polygon, Arbitrum, Avalanche or Sei). Errors are never charged: 400 bad input, 422 nothing found, 503 busy. Automated heuristic, may be wrong. Not financial advice.",
    "contact": {
      "name": "RugRadar",
      "url": "https://x402-seller-pmlm.onrender.com/rugradar"
    },
    "x-guidance": "RugRadar returns danger warnings for one token at a time. It does not certify a token or recommend a purchase.\n\nCall GET /rug-check, /token-safety, or /honeypot-check with token=<mint or 0x contract>. Optional chain=solana|base|bnb|ethereum|arbitrum (default solana; 0x addresses default to base). /token-safety returns the same report as /rug-check. /honeypot-check is the can-I-sell check. GET /watch is Solana-only and needs token, webhook, and optional hours=24|48.\n\nUnpaid calls return HTTP 402. Read the base64 x402 v2 challenge from the PAYMENT-REQUIRED header, sign one entry from accepts, and retry the same request with PAYMENT-SIGNATURE. After success, read PAYMENT-RESPONSE. The v1 X-PAYMENT header is not accepted. Failed calls are not charged.\n\naccepts lists USDC on Solana mainnet (fee payer covered, no SOL needed), Base, Polygon, Arbitrum, Avalanche, and Sei. Prices: $0.01 per check; /watch is $0.05 for 24h or $0.10 for 48h. Prefer /honeypot-check alone when you only need can-I-sell, and /watch instead of polling.\n"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://x402-seller-pmlm.onrender.com"
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "RugRadar",
      "description": "Token danger warnings paid per call with x402"
    }
  ],
